        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogFirstWax] = "Wax drops, pale as moonlight.",
        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogShopOpened] = "The Beekeeper's shop opens.",
        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogGloves] = "Padded gloves on. Much braver.",
        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogNet] = "A mesh net. Sweeping, not chasing.",
        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogVacuum] = "The vacuum hums. The bees seem to like it.",
        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogNewTool] = "A new tool.",
        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogWaxCatcher] = "The brass catcher gleams. Wax comes twice as fast.",
        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogCombsAvailable] = "The wax is gathering. Enough of it makes a comb.",
        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogCombBuiltFmt] = "A new comb. %@ bees move in.",
        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogWelcomeBackFmt] = "While you were away, the combs filled with %@ honey.",
        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogWelcomeBackNothing] = "The bees are glad you're back.",
        [StringKey.HelpBeekeeperObjective] = "Catch bees and look after a hive. The combs make honey, and the bees you haven't settled in a comb gather wax. Bees and wax build new combs, and a friendly bear trades Beebits for your honey. There is no score and no end: the hive simply grows at its own pace.",
        [StringKey.HelpBeekeeperHowToPlay] = "1. Catch Bee: each click catches free bees. With bare hands, a bee sometimes stings you and gets away.\n2. Honey: you start with one comb. Once you catch your first bee, every comb makes 0.2 honey a second, however many bees there are. When the combs are full, honey simply stops until you make room.\n3. Wax: a little wax gathers from the start, and every free bee adds a little more. Wax has its own, small store; when it's full, wax stops too.\n4. The Bear: once you hold 10 honey, a bear comes by. Trade 10 honey for 1 Beebit, or Trade all.\n5. The Shop: spend Beebits on better tools (each catches more bees, and none of them sting) and on the Wax-Catcher (twice the wax). Tools are bought in order.\n6. Combs: a new comb costs bees and wax, starting at 20 bees and 10 wax; the bees move in and stop being free bees. Each comb makes more honey and adds room for 300 honey and 2 wax, and each new comb costs a little more.\n7. Room: when a price needs more wax than the hive can hold, it says so. Honey Supers and Wax Trays at The Workbench, new combs and the storage upgrades in the Shop all make more room.",
        [StringKey.HelpBeekeeperAwayTitle] = "🌙 While You're Away",
        [StringKey.HelpBeekeeperAway] = "The hive keeps working while you play another game, and even while Honeycomb is closed, for up to 3 days. When the combs are full, no more honey is stored until you make room, and wax stops at its own store too, so more room means more to come back to. Nothing is sold while you're away. Your hive is saved automatically. New Game starts a brand-new hive, and asks first once you've caught your first bee.",
