        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogBeeBread] = "You pack pollen and honey into bee bread.",
        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogWoodenHive] = "You move the bees into a wooden hive. They seem pleased.",
        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogWaspRaidGuardsFmt] = "The wasp helps itself to %@ honey. The guards keep every bee safe.",
        [StringKey.BeekeeperLogShoeMissGuardsFmt] = "Missed. The wasp helps itself to %@ honey. The guards keep every bee safe.",
        [StringKey.HelpBeekeeperGardenTitle] = "🌱 The Garden",
        [StringKey.HelpBeekeeperGarden] = "The Hippies and the wasps sometimes give you a seed, and you can see what kind it is. Plant it in your bed (it grows one seed at a time) and wait: each plant takes its own time to sprout, even while the app is closed, and gives your hive a specialty.\n\nWildflowers and clover give foraging: a steady 3 pollen a minute each. Pollen and honey make bee bread at The Workbench, and bee bread plus wax pays for moving your bees into a wooden hive, where the combs make more honey. A bramble gives guarding: the combs make 25% more honey. The willow (about an hour) gives nursing: the queen lays 50% faster, and eats bee bread faster too. The poplar (about 6 hours, a seed from the wasps once you trade with them) gives resin: the bees gather propolis, which goes into candles and the Propolis Seal. Clover takes about 12 hours.\n\nPaper from the wasps buys the Beekeeper's Notebook, with a note about each thing your hive can do.",
